TITLE:Rec Dec Traditions
H1:Rec dec traditions: the agreed list <span class="draft">final · plan only</span>
SUB:The rec dec's own traditions, for when the deck is switched on (after Pillar 5's Steps 3 and 4). Agreed by the user in the survey (2026-10-19, 03:01) after three rounds: two traditions per sport room (one at the pool and one at the climbing wall), Wren talks small and often with a chief's talk every two weeks. Written by the Pillar 5 designer for lead 16. No game code.
NAV:final=The answers|rooms=Room by room|talks=Wren talks|week=The week|fit=Clash check|owner=For the rec deck|out=Dropped

<style>
.reading{border:1px solid var(--gold);background:rgba(233,196,106,.10);border-radius:10px;padding:10px 12px;font-size:14px}
.reading b{color:#f1dca0}
</style>

<section id="final">
  <h2>The user's answers (survey, 2026-10-19 03:01)</h2>
  <p class="reading"><b>Agreed:</b> each sport room has at most two traditions, counting the rec deck plan's own; the pool and the climbing wall have one each; Wren talks are small chats twice a week plus a chief's talk every two weeks, never like a Captain's address.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Did we read you right?</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>1. Do the rec plan's own traditions count?</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2. The river hall's three</td><td>"Paddle club and regatta": Glow paddle is out</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3. The pool's second</td><td>Neither: the pool keeps only Dawn swim for now</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4. The float room's second</td><td>Slow stretch</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Climbing wall</td><td>"Just one for this one": Wall night stays, Ring the bell is retired (below)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5. Non-sport traditions</td><td>None for now</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6. Chiefs' talks every two weeks</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7. Play your own Cup matches; give a talk yourself</td><td>Yes; yes</td></tr>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section id="rooms">
  <h2>Room by room</h2>
  <p class="note"><span class="tag new">gold</span> agreed in this plan · <span class="tag">teal</span> from the rec deck plan (v5), kept</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Room</th><th>Tradition</th><th>When</th><th>Who · what you do</th><th>You get</th><th>First</th></tr>
    <tr><td rowspan="2"><b>Lightdisc court</b></td><td><span class="tag">Winner Stays On</span></td><td>Sundays 11:30-16:30</td><td>Pell's chalkboard queue; tap the gate to play next</td><td>leisure, social; your name on the board for three wins in a row</td><td>Day 7</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="tag new">Lightdisc Cup</span></td><td>Every 4 weeks, Sunday 11:30-16:30, in Winner Stays On's place</td><td>Pell runs the bracket, pairs from each department; you enter with a friend and <b>play your own matches</b> live (the other pairs' results are worked out quietly)</td><td>leisure, social; a friendship step with your partner; department reputation if you go far; the foyer's Cup board</td><td>Day 28</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Pool</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Dawn swim</span></td><td>Tuesdays and Thursdays 06:15-06:45</td><td>Rina, before the infirmary opens; tap a lane</td><td>hygiene, energy; a friendship step with Rina over a few weeks</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td rowspan="2"><b>River hall (kayaks)</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Paddle club</span></td><td>Wednesdays 18:30-19:30</td><td>Chief Holt; the slow loop, then the fast run once he says you're ready (after three visits)</td><td>leisure; Holt warms to you</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="tag">River regatta</span></td><td>Every 4 weeks, Sunday 09:30-11:00</td><td>Heats of four round the loop, Holt's horn; watch from the bank or paddle the fun heat</td><td>leisure, social; the winner's pennant</td><td>Day 21</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Climbing wall</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Wall night</span></td><td>Tuesdays 18:30-19:45</td><td>Tomas belays; climb and ring the bell at the top</td><td>leisure; a friendship step with Tomas; your name on the season's bell board in the foyer</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td rowspan="2"><b>Float room</b></td><td><span class="tag new">Float hour</span></td><td>Wednesdays 21:30-22:15</td><td>Matthias Oduya dims the orbs; quiet music, no talking; tap to float</td><td>rest, mood (a calmer night's sleep)</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="tag new">Slow stretch</span></td><td>Sundays 08:30-09:15</td><td>Dr. Nandakumar leads a stretch at a fifth of gravity, 3 to 6 people; tap to join (the float animation, slower)</td><td>energy and mood for the day</td><td>Day 7</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Why Wall night over Ring the bell: you chose Wall night yourself, it's weekly, and it already rings the bell and keeps the season's bell board, so nothing of Ring the bell is lost.</p>
  <p>Not sport rooms: the auditorium keeps film night, talent night and the Captain's all-hands (the rec deck plan) and hosts the Wren talks (below). Nothing else for now.</p>
</section>

<section id="talks">
  <h2>Wren talks: small chats and chiefs' talks <span class="tag new">final</span></h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th></th><th>Small talk</th><th>Chief's talk</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>How often</b></td><td>Mondays and Thursdays, 19:00-19:40</td><td>Every two weeks, on a Thursday, 19:00-19:45, in place of that Thursday's small talk (and Day 8, below)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Who speaks</b></td><td>Any crew member, juniors included, about something they know or love</td><td>A department chief (or senior crew like the head of Survey): their department's best story</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Where</b></td><td>A ring of eight chairs on the auditorium stage, house dark, the stars behind; extras sit on the stage edge; tea from the utility room's kettle</td><td>The auditorium's seats, house lights half up, the speaker on a stool at the front of the stage (no lectern)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>How many</b></td><td>4 to 10</td><td>20 to 40 (a gathering, exempt from the deck's cap like talent night)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>How it goes</b></td><td>Chat; anyone can ask anything</td><td>About 25 minutes, then questions; no introductions, no Commander, never the Captain</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>You</b></td><td>Listen (the short meeting panel); ask one question for a friendship step with the speaker</td><td>Listen; one question, and a chief remembers who asked</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Skips:</b> the career's big days (1, 9-11, 15-16, 22-23, 26) and the storm (4-5), as v2 did. So the first four weeks have three talks (two of them chiefs'); from Day 29 there are two a week.</li>
    <li><b>Every Monday and Thursday has a talk</b> unless it's one of those skip days. The rota lists every talk day: in Days 1-28 only 8, 18 and 25 are clear (Mondays 1, 15, 22 and Thursdays 4, 11 are skipped); from Day 29 it's every Monday and Thursday.</li>
    <li><b>You give one:</b> once you're an Engine Specialist, after the career arc, you're asked to give a small talk ("What I learned in my first month") (the user: yes).</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>The rota, the first seven weeks</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Day</th><th>Size</th><th>Speaker</th><th>The talk</th></tr>
    <tr><td>8 Mon</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Dr. Imra Sato, head of Survey</td><td>"What lives between the stars": the creature everyone saw swim off at dinner (it left at 18:40). A one-off big Monday, since the whole ship wants to ask</td></tr>
    <tr><td>18 Thu</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Chief Calder, Works</td><td>"The Wren's first refit" (ends 19:45, before Echo Signal at 20:30)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>25 Thu</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Tomas (a junior, climbing)</td><td>"Reading a route": what the hold colours mean, with a hold passed round</td></tr>
    <tr><td>29 Mon</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Yara Esposito (Stores)</td><td>"Where every crate goes": the Wednesday delivery, crate by crate</td></tr>
    <tr><td>32 Thu</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Chief Bram Holt, Watch</td><td>"The oldest log in the Watch office": the night the Wren's first crew nearly lost the lift</td></tr>
    <tr><td>36 Mon</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Maeve Volkov (rec dec machines)</td><td>"How the float room floats": the gravity plates, and why a fifth (the evening after crew rotation day, an easy first evening for new crew)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>39 Thu</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Zeke Torres (Works, engine)</td><td>"How a drive coil sings": why the engine room hums in three notes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>43 Mon</td><td><span class="tag">small</span></td><td>Chef Auda Brennan (Galley)</td><td>"A spice for every port": three jars to sniff</td></tr>
    <tr><td>46 Thu</td><td><span class="tag new">chief's</span></td><td>Comms Chief Lucia Ferreira</td><td>"Messages that came home late": the longest a letter has taken to reach the Wren</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Then small talks from Pell ("Every disc trick I know"), Rina, the bunkmates, Envoy Saruth (a Veyli story, if you know them well) and you; chiefs' talks from Dr. Nandakumar (after the Wren cough, Days 50-53) and the chiefs again with a new story after about ten weeks.</p>
</section>

<section id="week">
  <h2>The week</h2>
  <p class="note">Only the rec dec. <span class="tag new">gold</span> agreed here · <span class="tag">teal</span> rec deck plan. "4-wk" runs every four weeks.</p>
  <div class="week">
    <div class="day"><h4>Monday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Small talk 19:00</span></p><p>the Captain's all-hands 17:45 (first Monday of a season only)</p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Tuesday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag new">Wall night 18:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Wednesday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Paddle club 18:30</span> <span class="tag new">Float hour 21:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Thursday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag new">Small talk 19:00, or a chief's talk (every 2 weeks)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Friday</h4><p>nothing of the rec dec's own (the ship's Friday jam and tap night elsewhere)</p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Saturday</h4><p><span class="tag">Film night 20:00</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Sunday</h4><p><span class="tag new">Slow stretch 08:30</span> <span class="tag">Regatta 09:30 (4-wk)</span> <span class="tag">Winner Stays On 11:30</span> <span class="tag new">Lightdisc Cup 11:30 (4-wk, in its place)</span> <span class="tag">Talent night 19:30 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="fit">
  <h2>Clash check</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Rooms:</b> no two share a room at once. The float room's two are Wednesday night and Sunday morning; Slow stretch ends 09:15, before the regatta (a different room) at 09:30. The auditorium: talks Mon and Thu 19:00 (small on the stage, chiefs' in the seats, never both at once), the all-hands Mon 17:45-18:10, film night Sat, talent night Sun.</li>
    <li><b>Numbers:</b> each draws 3 to 10, inside the rec dec's evening cap of about 15; the Cup, Winner Stays On, the regatta, the chiefs' talks and the shows are gatherings.</li>
    <li><b>Events plan (approved v4):</b> Day 4-5 storm: no talk that week; Dawn swim on Day 4 is before it. Day 8: the creature leaves 18:40, Sato's talk is 19:00. Day 18: Calder's talk ends 19:45, Echo Signal is 20:30. Day 21: the regatta (09:30-11:00) ends before the distress call (11:30-16:30), which pauses Winner Stays On. Day 24: Loss of Power is a morning; Paddle club and Float hour run that evening. Day 25: the inspector is daytime.</li>
    <li><b>Career:</b> talks skip the big days; the weekly sport ones run as usual but aren't pushed at you on those days (no Mail nudge).</li>
    <li><b>Mini-games:</b> the user wants the wall, the pool and the kayaks to become mini-games like Lightdisc; that has <a href="https://claude.ai/artifact/Ubn2MJvidnuK1awcx2gKMP" target="_blank" rel="noopener">its own plan</a> (<code>plans/rec-minigames-plan.html</code>). Until they're built, these traditions use the rec deck's tap animations.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="owner">
  <h2>For the rec deck plan's owner</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Ring the bell is retired</b> (the climbing wall keeps one tradition, Wall night). The season's bell board in the foyer stays and fills from Wall night.</li>
    <li><b>The regatta now stands alone</b> on its Sunday mornings (every 4 weeks from Day 21); the Sundays in between have no 09:30 river or wall event.</li>
    <li>Everything else in the rec deck plan's traditions (Winner Stays On, film night, talent night, the all-hands) is unchanged.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="out">
  <h2>Dropped along the way</h2>
  <p>Rookie court, Open stage, Lanes night, Zero-G games, Season splash (v1); Glow paddle, Ring dive, Captain's lengths, Triple tries (v3); Junior night, Birthday bell, Beach stories, Sing-along, Night-shift matinee, Kit mend night (v2 candidates); Ring the bell (from the rec deck plan).</p>
</section>
